The patch adds a loop to free each allocated page and then frees the `pages` array itself before returning from the error path. This ensures that all memory allocated by `btrfs_uring_read_extent()` is properly released when the function fails, preventing memory leaks. Additionally, initializing `pages = NULL` (not shown here but in the full patch) avoids a potential double-free or use-after-free if the early allocation fails.

